WEBVTT

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:17.182
Missing in Sydney by Andrea M.

00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:18.612
Hutchinson.

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:28.230
Copyright, Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:36.656
Listening activity.

00:00:36.716 --> 00:00:38.807
One.

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:41.838
I wouldn't want to do that.

00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:46.539
The idea of jumping off a bridge terrifies me.

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:48.870
Two.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:59.492
When I finish school, I want to spend a year going round the world, visiting as many different countries as I can.

00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:01.612
Three.

00:01:01.672 --> 00:01:07.294
I get up early on Saturday morning so that I can get all my homework done.

00:01:07.354 --> 00:01:10.906
Then I'm free for the rest of the weekend.

00:01:10.965 --> 00:01:13.176
Four.

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:19.319
I tried it last summer for the first time when we were on holiday at the seaside.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.830
The water was too dirty to be able to see much though.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.062
Five.

00:01:26.122 --> 00:01:29.120
It's great now with digital cameras.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:32.248
As you can just delete a picture that's no good.

00:01:32.308 --> 00:01:36.998
I mean, you don't have to pay to get it developed first.

00:01:37.058 --> 00:01:39.299
6.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.880
This is my favourite thing to do on Saturday evenings.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:48.581
I go to a local one with a friend and we dance all night.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:53.652
I usually get home around 4am.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:02:00.674
Chapter 1 A Christmas party.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:04.705
Are you coming to this beach party, Amy?

00:02:04.765 --> 00:02:06.356
Shouted Claire.

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:09.627
If you don't hurry up, we'll miss the bus.

00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:12.938
There isn't another one for an hour after that.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.299
Said Lisa.

00:02:14.358 --> 00:02:16.329
I'm coming.

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:20.071
Said Amy, finally coming out of the bathroom.

00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:22.872
Well, how do I look?

00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:27.522
She asked her two best friends with a big smile.

00:02:27.582 --> 00:02:32.956
Claire and Lisa looked at each other and started to laugh.

00:02:33.016 --> 00:02:34.797
What is it?

00:02:34.857 --> 00:02:35.918
asked Amy.

00:02:35.978 --> 00:02:37.088
Worried.

00:02:37.148 --> 00:02:41.812
Amy, we're going to the Christmas party on Bondi Beach.

00:02:41.872 --> 00:02:43.524
Not to a nightclub.

00:02:43.584 --> 00:02:44.725
Said Lisa.

00:02:44.785 --> 00:02:47.857
You can't stand up now in those shoes.

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.229
How are you going to dance all night?

00:02:50.289 --> 00:02:51.450
Loved Claire.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.132
You never know who we might meet.

00:02:54.192 --> 00:02:55.316
Replied Amy.

00:02:55.376 --> 00:02:59.500
Just because you two don't understand anything about fashion.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.842
Come on, let's go!

00:03:01.902 --> 00:03:06.394
There were a lot of people already at the beach when they arrived.

00:03:06.454 --> 00:03:13.528
The music was loud, and even though the sun was starting to go down, it was still warm.

00:03:13.588 --> 00:03:18.280
This was where the three best friends wanted to be.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.305
For two years they planned this holiday.

00:03:22.365 --> 00:03:33.173
And finally, after hours of studying for exams, on Claire's 18th birthday, their plane took off from London's Heathrow Airport.

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.965
Destination, Australia.

00:03:37.025 --> 00:03:51.652
Amy cuddled koala bears, Lisa bungee jumped off a bridge in Cairns, and Claire made them wake up really early so that she could take photos of Ayers Rock at dawn.

00:03:51.712 --> 00:04:00.198
but they all agreed snorkelling in the clear waters of the Great Barrier Reef was the best bit.

00:04:00.258 --> 00:04:06.082
And now they were in Sydney where they planned to celebrate New Year.

00:04:06.142 --> 00:04:14.616
Next September, after this year of travelling, Claire was going to study art and photography at university.

00:04:14.676 --> 00:04:17.488
Claire wanted to become a photographer.

00:04:17.548 --> 00:04:20.884
It was the only job she wanted to do.

00:04:20.943 --> 00:04:27.282
Lisa was thinking about joining the police, although her dad didn't know it yet.

00:04:27.342 --> 00:04:31.366
He wanted her to study law and become a lawyer.

00:04:31.426 --> 00:04:39.735
And Amy wanted to marry someone who was rich so that she could go shopping all day, every day.

00:04:39.795 --> 00:04:46.584
But now, they still had another six months left of parties and fun.

00:04:46.643 --> 00:04:48.296
Mmm.

00:04:48.356 --> 00:04:51.137
Look at all that delicious food.

00:04:51.197 --> 00:04:54.887
Barbecued sausages, burgers and steaks.

00:04:54.947 --> 00:04:56.778
Let's have something to eat.

00:04:56.838 --> 00:04:58.188
Said Claire.

00:04:58.248 --> 00:04:59.558
Amy.

00:04:59.618 --> 00:05:00.808
Claire.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.579
Interrupted Lisa.

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:04.359
They looked at her.

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:07.730
It was obvious that she wanted something.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.010
I've forgotten my purse.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.020
Can I borrow $10?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.706
I've only got a few coins on me.

00:05:14.766 --> 00:05:16.531
Again.

00:05:16.591 --> 00:05:19.643
You always forget to bring enough money.

00:05:19.703 --> 00:05:20.954
Said Claire.

00:05:21.014 --> 00:05:22.285
Yes.

00:05:22.345 --> 00:05:26.948
And you haven't given me back the five dollars you owe me for dinner the other night.

00:05:27.008 --> 00:05:28.250
Said Amy.

00:05:28.309 --> 00:05:30.491
Lisa looked upset.

00:05:30.551 --> 00:05:33.463
She didn't plan to forget her money.

00:05:33.523 --> 00:05:35.064
It doesn't matter.

00:05:35.124 --> 00:05:36.225
She said.

00:05:36.285 --> 00:05:37.276
Angry.

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:40.038
She went over to another group of friends.

00:05:40.098 --> 00:05:43.246
Don't ask me for anything in future.

00:05:43.306 --> 00:05:44.643
Lisa!

00:05:44.703 --> 00:05:46.614
shouted Amy and Claire.

00:05:46.674 --> 00:05:49.367
But she just ignored them.

00:05:49.427 --> 00:05:58.254
Later, as the party was finishing, Amy and Claire waited for Lisa so they could go back to the youth hostel together.

00:05:58.314 --> 00:06:00.596
There was a cool wind.

00:06:00.656 --> 00:06:03.559
I think there might be a storm later on.

00:06:03.618 --> 00:06:07.992
I've got a headache and I'll always get a headache before a storm.

00:06:08.052 --> 00:06:09.153
Said Amy.

00:06:09.213 --> 00:06:11.607
Oh, where's Lisa?

00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:14.359
Maybe she went back to the youth hostel.

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:17.230
The last time I saw her was when we argued.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.250
Said Claire.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.691
What time is it?

00:06:19.751 --> 00:06:21.001
Ask Amy.

00:06:21.061 --> 00:06:22.372
Two o'clock.

00:06:22.432 --> 00:06:23.732
Answered Claire.

00:06:23.792 --> 00:06:26.914
Perhaps she's at the hostel in bed.

00:06:26.974 --> 00:06:28.684
Yes, come on.

00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:33.076
Everyone else has gone and my feet are really hurting.

00:06:33.136 --> 00:06:35.887
I told you not to wear those shoes.

00:06:35.947 --> 00:06:37.568
Laughed Claire.

00:06:37.628 --> 00:06:46.927
When they got back, Amy opened the door to their room with a nervous smile and said, You missed a great party.

00:06:46.987 --> 00:06:51.390
But then she realised that Lisa wasn't in bed.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.400
She wasn't in the bathroom either.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.962
Maybe she's met someone.

00:06:57.022 --> 00:06:58.672
Said Claire hopefully.

00:06:58.732 --> 00:06:59.893
Maybe.

00:06:59.953 --> 00:07:01.294
Said Amy.

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:03.134
Let's go to bed.

00:07:03.194 --> 00:07:08.716
In the morning she'll tell us all about some gorgeous Australian that she met at the party.

00:07:08.776 --> 00:07:11.917
said Claire, but she didn't seem sure.

00:07:11.976 --> 00:07:13.357
Maybe.

00:07:13.417 --> 00:07:14.848
Said Amy.

00:07:14.907 --> 00:07:23.562
And as she heard the first sound of thunder, she realized that her feet didn't hurt anymore.

00:07:23.622 --> 00:07:27.274
Chapter Two.

00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:29.904
Where's Lisa?

00:07:29.964 --> 00:07:36.308
The girl's youth hostel was in the center of Sydney, opposite Hyde Park.

00:07:36.368 --> 00:07:42.100
When Amy woke up early the next morning, she was happy they had their own room.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:47.652
In some hostels, the rooms were bigger you had to share with a lot of other people.

00:07:47.712 --> 00:07:52.744
Today, she didn't feel like being polite or nice to anyone.

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:59.366
Their room was very small for three people, but there was a nice view of the park below.

00:07:59.426 --> 00:08:04.463
Lisa liked sitting in the park when she wanted to write in her diary.

00:08:04.522 --> 00:08:11.262
But this morning, when Amy looked out towards the park, she could only see their friend, Jack.

00:08:11.322 --> 00:08:15.725
He was sitting alone, near the fountain, reading a book.

00:08:15.784 --> 00:08:18.656
It was a beautiful sunny day now.

00:08:18.716 --> 00:08:23.920
The storm of the night before was over, just like a bad dream.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.122
Claire, wake up.

00:08:26.182 --> 00:08:29.354
Said Amy, touching Claire on the shoulder.

00:08:29.414 --> 00:08:31.495
Another five minutes.

00:08:31.555 --> 00:08:34.653
Said Claire, pulling the sheet over her head.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:37.940
No, you've got to wake up now.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.341
Lisa's still not here.

00:08:40.401 --> 00:08:42.932
She didn't come back last night.

00:08:42.992 --> 00:08:47.434
Claire immediately threw the sheets off her and sat up.

00:08:47.494 --> 00:08:51.626
Let's get dressed and we'll go downstairs and have some breakfast.

00:08:51.686 --> 00:08:52.626
Said Claire.

00:08:52.686 --> 00:08:56.468
Perhaps Lisa got up early and is already there.

00:08:56.528 --> 00:09:01.770
Five minutes later, while they were going downstairs, they met Jack.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.327
Jack was travelling as well.

00:09:04.387 --> 00:09:10.584
He arrived in Sydney on the same day as the girls, and they met as they were checking into the hostel.

00:09:10.644 --> 00:09:20.958
The four of them soon became friends, and they often spent evenings together, talking until late, sharing pizza and beer in the hostel's garden.

00:09:21.018 --> 00:09:23.938
Now it seemed like he was in a hurry.

00:09:23.998 --> 00:09:25.759
Hello, Jack.

00:09:25.819 --> 00:09:27.989
Have you seen Lisa this morning?

00:09:28.049 --> 00:09:29.000
asked Claire.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.250
No, I haven't.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.100
She's not in the dining hall.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.609
Why?

00:09:33.669 --> 00:09:36.238
It's probably nothing.

00:09:36.298 --> 00:09:39.859
If you see her, tell her that we're looking for her.

00:09:39.919 --> 00:09:40.970
Said Amy.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:44.241
I'm leaving today, so I probably won't.

00:09:44.301 --> 00:09:46.212
But if I see her...

00:09:46.272 --> 00:09:50.154
Sorry, I'm in a hurry, and I must go and pack my things.

00:09:50.214 --> 00:09:55.556
Before they could say goodbye, he ran by them and into his room.

00:09:55.616 --> 00:09:57.477
Jack was right.

00:09:57.537 --> 00:10:00.116
There was nobody in the dining hall.

00:10:00.176 --> 00:10:02.296
It's 715.

00:10:02.356 --> 00:10:04.016
It's still early.

00:10:04.076 --> 00:10:08.978
If we sit over there by the window, we'll see her when she comes back.

00:10:09.038 --> 00:10:11.298
Do you want something to eat?

00:10:11.358 --> 00:10:12.638
asked Claire.

00:10:12.698 --> 00:10:15.279
No, I'm not hungry.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:17.790
I think I'll just have some orange juice.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.410
said Amy.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.292
In silence, Amy and Claire waited.

00:10:23.352 --> 00:10:29.186
Every time the door opened, they both looked up, hoping that it was Lisa.

00:10:29.246 --> 00:10:36.724
At eight o'clock, the dining hall was starting to get busy and their glasses of orange juice were still full.

00:10:36.784 --> 00:10:40.597
Come on, I can't just sit here anymore.

00:10:40.657 --> 00:10:47.293
Let's go back upstairs to the room and try to call her on her mobile, said Claire.

00:10:47.353 --> 00:10:53.988
Back in the room, Amy dialed 387-452-9113.

00:10:54.048 --> 00:11:02.012
She walked up and down the room, waiting for the number to start ringing.

00:11:02.072 --> 00:11:04.704
Okay, it's ringing.

00:11:04.764 --> 00:11:07.156
She said to Claire with a nervous smile.

00:11:07.216 --> 00:11:08.156
Shh!

00:11:08.216 --> 00:11:11.268
Said Claire suddenly.

00:11:11.328 --> 00:11:14.040
What is it?

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.630
Said Amy.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:20.674
She watched Claire go over to the bedside table and open the drawer.

00:11:20.734 --> 00:11:26.387
As she opened it, the ringtone of Lisa's phone filled the room.

00:11:26.447 --> 00:11:29.998
Amy hung up the phone, disappointed.

00:11:30.058 --> 00:11:31.308
Amy!

00:11:31.368 --> 00:11:32.538
Look!

00:11:32.598 --> 00:11:35.529
Lisa's purse is in here too.

00:11:35.589 --> 00:11:40.290
So, Lisa hasn't got her mobile or any money with her.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.320
Said Amy.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.351
Oh Claire, where could she be?

00:11:44.411 --> 00:11:46.731
This isn't like her at all.

00:11:46.791 --> 00:11:50.812
What are we going to do?

00:11:50.872 --> 00:11:55.554
Listening activity.

00:11:55.614 --> 00:11:58.535
What is happening?

00:11:58.595 --> 00:12:01.716
When did you last see her?

00:12:01.776 --> 00:12:04.418
Where are you now?

00:12:04.478 --> 00:12:07.380
What time is it there?

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.240
Did you call the police?

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:14.383
Did you try to ring her on her mobile?

00:12:14.443 --> 00:12:21.356
What are you going to do now?

00:12:21.416 --> 00:12:29.068
About half past eight in the morning.

00:12:29.128 --> 00:12:30.928
Two.

00:12:30.988 --> 00:12:34.308
At the youth hostel with Amy.

00:12:34.368 --> 00:12:36.049
Three.

00:12:36.109 --> 00:12:37.859
I'm not sure.

00:12:37.919 --> 00:12:41.220
I'll talk to Amy and see what she thinks.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.150
Four.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.090
It's Lisa.

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:47.560
She's disappeared.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.601
Five.

00:12:49.661 --> 00:12:54.052
Last night at a party on Bondi Beach.

00:12:54.112 --> 00:12:56.097
Six.

00:12:56.157 --> 00:12:58.232
No, not yet.

00:12:58.292 --> 00:13:03.214
I mean, maybe we're going to if she doesn't come back soon.

00:13:03.274 --> 00:13:05.324
Seven?

00:13:05.384 --> 00:13:09.035
Yes, but she hasn't got it with her.

00:13:09.095 --> 00:13:13.696
It's here in the room at the hostel.

00:13:13.756 --> 00:13:18.438
Listening activity.

00:13:18.498 --> 00:13:20.184
One.

00:13:20.243 --> 00:13:24.960
Yes, we're definitely going to go there when we're in Sydney.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:28.711
I can't wait to do some sunbathing and surfing.

00:13:28.771 --> 00:13:36.022
It'll seem strange, though, to be doing this sort of thing at Christmas time when it's freezing in Britain.

00:13:36.082 --> 00:13:38.083
Two.

00:13:38.143 --> 00:13:46.942
I walked across it when I was in Sydney, but I didn't want to go up to the top, even though the views are meant to be fantastic.

00:13:47.002 --> 00:13:53.684
135 metres above sea level is too high for me.

00:13:53.704 --> 00:13:54.234
3.

00:13:54.294 --> 00:14:00.468
It took us nearly the whole day actually, as we stopped for a swim a few times on the way.

00:14:00.528 --> 00:14:05.952
We were too tired to walk back again, so we cheated and got the boat.

00:14:06.012 --> 00:14:07.994
4.

00:14:08.054 --> 00:14:11.306
This is my favourite part of Sydney.

00:14:11.366 --> 00:14:15.888
There's lots going on here, loads of restaurants and bars.

00:14:15.948 --> 00:14:19.228
I love coming here in the evenings.

00:14:19.288 --> 00:14:21.308
5.

00:14:21.368 --> 00:14:25.139
We saw La Trivieta there when we were in Sydney.

00:14:25.199 --> 00:14:35.052
It wasn't a very good production, but it was a great experience to be in such an amazing building.

00:14:35.112 --> 00:14:40.904
searching for Lisa.

00:14:40.964 --> 00:14:47.398
For the next four hours, Amy and Claire walked around Sydney.

00:14:47.458 --> 00:14:56.512
They even walked the 10-kilometre manly scenic walkway because they knew that Lisa liked the views from there.

00:14:56.572 --> 00:15:01.416
They asked everybody they knew, have you seen Lisa?

00:15:01.476 --> 00:15:04.404
And they showed her photo to strangers.

00:15:04.464 --> 00:15:10.102
This is useless, said Amy, looking at the view of Sydney Harbour.

00:15:10.162 --> 00:15:12.342
Nobody has seen her.

00:15:12.402 --> 00:15:15.473
Why don't we go back to Bondi Beach?

00:15:15.533 --> 00:15:19.324
Maybe somebody will remember her from the party last night.

00:15:19.384 --> 00:15:20.544
Said Claire.

00:15:20.604 --> 00:15:21.504
Okay.

00:15:21.564 --> 00:15:22.555
Agreed Amy.

00:15:22.615 --> 00:15:28.176
But if nobody there knows where she is, I think we should go to the police.

00:15:28.236 --> 00:15:34.949
Amy and Claire walked up and down the beach, showing everyone Lisa's photo.

00:15:35.009 --> 00:15:36.882
It was two o'clock.

00:15:36.942 --> 00:15:38.952
The sun was hot.

00:15:39.012 --> 00:15:41.504
I need to put some sun cream on.

00:15:41.564 --> 00:15:44.536
Amy said, looking at her red arms.

00:15:44.596 --> 00:15:48.718
Do you want to go to that bar over there and have some lunch?

00:15:48.778 --> 00:15:51.379
Then we can go to the police station.

00:15:51.439 --> 00:15:52.790
Said Claire.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:56.132
Do you think something has happened to her?

00:15:56.192 --> 00:16:02.510
Before Amy could answer, a blonde Australian girl came over to take their order.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:08.451
Can we have one tuna salad, one chicken salad, and a large bottle of water please?

00:16:08.511 --> 00:16:09.742
asked Claire.

00:16:09.802 --> 00:16:12.594
Were you here yesterday at the party?

00:16:12.654 --> 00:16:14.586
asked Amy hopefully.

00:16:14.646 --> 00:16:19.170
The waitress was very small and Amy thought she recognized her.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.622
Yes, but I was working.

00:16:21.682 --> 00:16:23.534
Did you see our friend?

00:16:23.594 --> 00:16:26.366
asked Claire, showing her the photo.

00:16:26.426 --> 00:16:31.281
The waitress took the photo from Claire and looked at it carefully.

00:16:31.341 --> 00:16:34.753
Amy and Claire expected her to say no.

00:16:34.813 --> 00:16:36.744
But then she smiled.

00:16:36.804 --> 00:16:38.105
Ah, yes.

00:16:38.165 --> 00:16:39.685
I remember her.

00:16:39.745 --> 00:16:43.397
I remember thinking how pretty and tall she was.

00:16:43.457 --> 00:16:46.538
Amy and Claire became very interested.

00:16:46.598 --> 00:16:49.359
You don't remember if she was with anyone.

00:16:49.419 --> 00:16:50.510
Asked Claire.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.901
What time was it when you saw her?

00:16:52.961 --> 00:16:54.542
Interrupted Amy.

00:16:54.602 --> 00:16:56.492
It was about eleven.

00:16:56.552 --> 00:16:59.504
And yes, she was talking to a man.

00:16:59.564 --> 00:17:00.945
He had black hair.

00:17:01.004 --> 00:17:05.967
Amy opened her mouth to ask another question, but the waitress stopped her.

00:17:06.027 --> 00:17:08.829
I'm sorry, but that's all I can remember.

00:17:08.889 --> 00:17:10.560
I didn't see his face.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:11.900
It was dark.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.662
With a kind smile, she went to get their food.

00:17:15.722 --> 00:17:17.733
Who's got black hair?

00:17:17.793 --> 00:17:19.794
said Amy excitedly.

00:17:19.854 --> 00:17:24.446
But before she thought of anyone, her mobile started ringing.

00:17:24.506 --> 00:17:27.507
Her hand was shaking when she answered.

00:17:27.568 --> 00:17:30.646
Hello?

00:17:30.706 --> 00:17:35.035
Listening activity.

00:17:35.095 --> 00:17:39.208
1 Have you seen Lisa?

00:17:39.268 --> 00:17:45.500
2 Why don't we go back to Bondi Beach?

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:50.862
3 Do you want to go to that bar over there and have some lunch?

00:17:50.923 --> 00:17:56.636
4 Do you think something has happened to her?

00:17:56.696 --> 00:18:01.930
5 Were you here yesterday at the party?

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.923
Six.

00:18:03.982 --> 00:18:06.854
Did you see our friend?

00:18:06.914 --> 00:18:08.884
Seven.

00:18:08.944 --> 00:18:12.686
You don't remember if she was with anyone.

00:18:12.746 --> 00:18:14.326
Eight.

00:18:14.386 --> 00:18:17.638
What time was it when you saw her?

00:18:17.698 --> 00:18:19.298
Nine.

00:18:19.358 --> 00:18:23.310
Who's got black hair?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.991
Chapter Four.

00:18:27.051 --> 00:18:30.267
Lisa makes a phone call.

00:18:30.327 --> 00:18:36.284
Breathless, Lisa ran as fast as she could towards the telephone box.

00:18:36.344 --> 00:18:42.676
Her ankle hurt from when he pulled her into the house, but there was no time to think of that now.

00:18:42.736 --> 00:18:45.236
Only a few more steps.

00:18:45.296 --> 00:18:50.268
Oh, why did I have that stupid argument with Amy and Claire?

00:18:50.328 --> 00:18:52.608
Why did I forget my purse?

00:18:52.668 --> 00:18:54.539
Why did I trust him?

00:18:54.599 --> 00:18:57.628
She thought, with tears in her eyes.

00:18:57.688 --> 00:19:02.530
Looking constantly over her shoulder, she lifted the receiver.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:09.898
The inside of the telephone box was dirty and covered in graffiti, but luckily the phone was working.

00:19:09.958 --> 00:19:16.406
She put her only money, a $1 coin, into the phone and dialed Amy's number.

00:19:16.466 --> 00:19:19.569
Please pick up the phone, please.

00:19:19.629 --> 00:19:20.683
She thought.

00:19:20.742 --> 00:19:25.660
On the second ring, Amy answered and Lisa started crying.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:29.794
Amy, I'm so glad you're there.

00:19:29.854 --> 00:19:32.476
Lisa, is that you?

00:19:32.536 --> 00:19:34.337
Where are you?

00:19:34.397 --> 00:19:35.838
I don't know.

00:19:35.858 --> 00:19:37.750
I need your help.

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:44.280
The line was bad and because Lisa was crying, it was difficult to understand what she was saying.

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:45.436
I'm sorry.

00:19:45.456 --> 00:19:47.917
There are things you don't know.

00:19:47.937 --> 00:19:52.080
Things I have never told you about my dad.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.991
Lisa, that's not important.

00:19:55.051 --> 00:19:56.321
Calm down.

00:19:56.381 --> 00:19:59.836
Tell us where you are and we'll come and get you.

00:19:59.896 --> 00:20:01.531
Oh, please, hurry.

00:20:01.551 --> 00:20:03.472
He's coming after me.

00:20:03.532 --> 00:20:04.362
He...

00:20:04.423 --> 00:20:07.504
Lisa, what are you trying to say?

00:20:07.564 --> 00:20:09.575
Did someone hurt you at the party?

00:20:09.595 --> 00:20:15.078
He wants money from my dad to make him pay.

00:20:15.098 --> 00:20:16.080
Who?

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.871
Lisa, you're scaring me.

00:20:18.931 --> 00:20:22.423
Tell me where you are and then phone the police.

00:20:22.483 --> 00:20:25.865
Amy said, I don't know the number.

00:20:25.925 --> 00:20:28.616
I don't know where I am.

00:20:28.676 --> 00:20:32.218
Suddenly, Lisa went comb.

00:20:32.279 --> 00:20:35.260
Somebody was standing behind her.

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:36.962
He was there.

00:20:37.022 --> 00:20:38.882
She could feel him.

00:20:38.942 --> 00:20:41.954
Lisa, are you still there?

00:20:42.014 --> 00:20:43.025
Lisa!

00:20:43.085 --> 00:20:44.635
shouted Amy.

00:20:44.696 --> 00:20:50.969
Lisa stood terrified as she watched him take the phone from her and hang up.

00:20:51.029 --> 00:20:53.145
He was smiling at her.

00:20:53.205 --> 00:20:56.011
But it wasn't a nice smile.

00:20:56.071 --> 00:21:00.083
It was an evil, mad smile.

00:21:00.143 --> 00:21:04.115
Why didn't you stay at the house, Lisa?

00:21:04.175 --> 00:21:06.366
But it doesn't matter.

00:21:06.426 --> 00:21:09.097
Nobody will ever find you.

00:21:09.158 --> 00:21:17.611
Putting a baseball cap over his black hair, he pulled her out of the telephone box.

00:21:17.671 --> 00:21:22.094
Listening activity.

00:21:22.154 --> 00:21:24.093
One.

00:21:24.153 --> 00:21:27.822
They try to catch people who break the law.

00:21:27.883 --> 00:21:34.124
In Britain, they wear dark blue uniforms and they don't usually carry guns.

00:21:34.184 --> 00:21:42.906
This crime is when you finish another person's life.

00:21:42.966 --> 00:21:50.582
This is the person who decides what happens to someone who has broken the law.

00:21:50.642 --> 00:21:57.820
This is the place where people are put if they have broken the law in a serious way.

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:04.234
They can't leave until they have been there for a specified period of time.

00:22:04.294 --> 00:22:16.210
5 This is when someone takes another person by force and then asks for money to let the person go.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:26.973
Chapter 5 At the Police Station We need to talk to somebody urgently.

00:22:27.033 --> 00:22:32.024
Amy told the policeman in the front office before he could even say hello.

00:22:32.084 --> 00:22:36.666
Something has happened to our friend Lisa and we need your help.

00:22:36.726 --> 00:22:38.947
She went missing last night.

00:22:39.007 --> 00:22:41.098
You must help us find her.

00:22:41.158 --> 00:22:42.318
Said Claire.

00:22:42.378 --> 00:22:45.559
We got a phone call from her five minutes ago.

00:22:45.619 --> 00:22:46.669
Interrupted Amy.

00:22:46.729 --> 00:22:47.780
She's in trouble.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:48.590
Said Claire.

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:50.831
Somebody has kidnapped her.

00:22:50.891 --> 00:22:52.362
Shouted Amy.

00:22:52.423 --> 00:22:56.475
The officer looked confused and went inside.

00:22:56.535 --> 00:23:00.686
When he came back, there was another policeman with him.

00:23:00.746 --> 00:23:02.176
Good day.

00:23:02.236 --> 00:23:04.716
My name is Inspector Swanson.

00:23:04.776 --> 00:23:07.127
Would you like to come through here, please?

00:23:07.187 --> 00:23:11.088
He said, taking them into an untidy office.

00:23:11.148 --> 00:23:13.148
Please, take a seat.

00:23:13.208 --> 00:23:15.929
I understand that your friend is missing.

00:23:15.989 --> 00:23:17.259
What's her name?

00:23:17.319 --> 00:23:18.079
Lisa.

00:23:18.139 --> 00:23:20.610
Her name is Lisa McIntosh.

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.069
Said Claire.

00:23:22.129 --> 00:23:27.061
He sat down at his desk and started writing down the details.

00:23:27.121 --> 00:23:28.652
How old is she?

00:23:28.672 --> 00:23:30.604
18.

00:23:30.664 --> 00:23:32.835
She'll be 19 next month.

00:23:32.895 --> 00:23:35.868
Amy said, trying not to cry.

00:23:35.928 --> 00:23:39.470
Inspector Swanson smiled kindly at Amy.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:42.942
He could see that both the girls were very worried.

00:23:43.002 --> 00:23:46.144
What was she wearing when she went missing?

00:23:46.204 --> 00:23:49.376
She was wearing blue jeans and a pink t-shirt.

00:23:49.436 --> 00:23:50.438
Said Claire.

00:23:50.498 --> 00:23:53.439
Can you describe her to me?

00:23:53.499 --> 00:23:57.450
She has long, curly blonde hair and blue eyes.

00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:59.681
This is a photo of Lisa.

00:23:59.741 --> 00:24:02.962
Amy said and gave him one of their photos.

00:24:03.022 --> 00:24:08.114
She's very pretty and tall, about 1.75 metres.

00:24:08.174 --> 00:24:11.916
Amy said, remembering what the waitress said earlier.

00:24:11.976 --> 00:24:15.407
When was the last time you saw her?

00:24:15.467 --> 00:24:17.648
It was about 8.30 last night.

00:24:17.708 --> 00:24:19.367
said Claire.

00:24:19.427 --> 00:24:24.408
Are you sure she isn't with anyone she met at the party?

00:24:24.468 --> 00:24:26.459
A friend perhaps?

00:24:26.519 --> 00:24:30.710
Inspector Swanson looked at them very seriously.

00:24:30.770 --> 00:24:34.100
No, not without telling us first.

00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:36.991
Said Amy, shaking her head.

00:24:37.051 --> 00:24:40.031
We made a rule before we left England.

00:24:40.091 --> 00:24:46.883
If you want to stay out all night, then you have to tell the others where you're going, who with, and when you'll be back.

00:24:46.943 --> 00:24:48.262
Explained Claire.

00:24:48.322 --> 00:24:50.381
Lisa knows that rule.

00:24:50.441 --> 00:24:52.742
She knows we'll be worried.

00:24:52.802 --> 00:24:55.953
Inspector Swanson listened carefully.

00:24:56.013 --> 00:24:58.934
He thought they were telling him the truth.

00:24:58.994 --> 00:25:04.716
You told the other officer that somebody has kidnapped her.

00:25:04.776 --> 00:25:06.267
He said cautiously.

00:25:06.327 --> 00:25:07.237
Yes.

00:25:07.297 --> 00:25:09.538
The two girls said at the same time.

00:25:09.598 --> 00:25:13.039
That's a very serious thing to say.

00:25:13.099 --> 00:25:17.644
Swanson searched their eyes for any sign that they were lying.

00:25:17.704 --> 00:25:20.328
But they both looked back, honestly.

00:25:20.388 --> 00:25:23.249
Lisa told us that on the phone.

00:25:23.309 --> 00:25:26.180
So, you have spoken to Lisa?

00:25:26.240 --> 00:25:28.570
He asked, raising an eyebrow.

00:25:28.630 --> 00:25:31.481
Yes, about a quarter of an hour ago.

00:25:31.541 --> 00:25:33.932
Said Claire, looking at her watch.

00:25:33.992 --> 00:25:37.503
Why don't you send some people to look for her?

00:25:37.563 --> 00:25:40.043
Asked Amy, starting to get angry.

00:25:40.103 --> 00:25:47.072
They were wasting time, sitting here, filling in stupid forms when they could be looking for Lisa.

00:25:47.132 --> 00:25:51.340
Amy, said Claire, trying to calm her down.

00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:53.372
She turned to Swanson.

00:25:53.433 --> 00:25:57.566
I'm sorry, but we're really worried about Lisa.

00:25:57.625 --> 00:26:00.448
She said that a man was after her.

00:26:00.508 --> 00:26:02.609
A policeman knocked on the door.

00:26:02.629 --> 00:26:09.154
It's sorry to interrupt you, sir, but could I talk with you in private, please?

00:26:09.214 --> 00:26:10.264
He asked.

00:26:10.324 --> 00:26:11.456
I'm busy.

00:26:11.516 --> 00:26:12.846
Can't it wait?

00:26:12.906 --> 00:26:14.198
Said Swanson.

00:26:14.258 --> 00:26:16.186
It's very important, sir.

00:26:16.246 --> 00:26:20.234
said the policeman, and Swanson stood up.

00:26:20.254 --> 00:26:21.454
I won't be long.

00:26:21.514 --> 00:26:25.155
Can you finish filling in that form about Lisa, please?

00:26:25.215 --> 00:26:28.876
He told them, and went into another office.

00:26:28.936 --> 00:26:34.306
When he came back, his friendly eyes were dark with worry.

00:26:34.366 --> 00:26:36.267
Was that about Lisa?

00:26:36.327 --> 00:26:37.747
asked Claire.

00:26:37.807 --> 00:26:43.492
Swanson sat down and took a deep breath before speaking.

00:26:43.552 --> 00:26:49.018
that phone call was from Scotland Yard in England.

00:26:49.078 --> 00:26:55.290
Judge MacIntosh, the famous judge, has received a phone call.

00:26:55.350 --> 00:27:01.723
A man from Australia has told Judge MacIntosh that he has kidnapped his daughter.

00:27:01.783 --> 00:27:08.095
The kidnapper wants his father to be released from prison and $200,000 or...

00:27:08.155 --> 00:27:09.395
What?

00:27:09.456 --> 00:27:14.900
...asked Claire and Amy at the same time.

00:27:14.960 --> 00:27:20.096
Or he will kill Lisa.

00:27:20.156 --> 00:27:24.708
Listening activity.

00:27:24.769 --> 00:27:26.500
One.

00:27:26.560 --> 00:27:29.752
Somebody has kidnapped her.

00:27:29.812 --> 00:27:31.222
Two.

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:33.464
She's in trouble.

00:27:33.524 --> 00:27:35.424
Three.

00:27:35.484 --> 00:27:40.358
Are you sure she isn't with anyone she met at the party?

00:27:40.418 --> 00:27:42.385
Four.

00:27:42.446 --> 00:27:45.554
We made a rule before we left England.

00:27:45.615 --> 00:27:53.552
If you want to stay out all night, then you have to tell the others where you're going, who with and when you'll be back.

00:27:53.612 --> 00:27:55.314
Five.

00:27:55.374 --> 00:27:59.898
That's a very serious thing to say.

00:27:59.958 --> 00:28:01.940
Six.

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:06.204
Why don't you send some people to look for her?

00:28:06.264 --> 00:28:07.986
Seven.

00:28:08.046 --> 00:28:12.467
I'm sorry, but we're really worried about Lisa.

00:28:12.527 --> 00:28:17.077
She said that a man was after her.

00:28:17.138 --> 00:28:20.918
Chapter 6.

00:28:20.978 --> 00:28:23.408
The Truth.

00:28:23.468 --> 00:28:31.480
Swanson ordered Amy and Claire to stay in his office while he organized his offices.

00:28:31.540 --> 00:28:37.564
Judge McIntosh, Lisa's father, was already on a plane with the money.

00:28:37.625 --> 00:28:42.570
Everybody seemed to be busy doing something to help Lisa.

00:28:42.630 --> 00:28:47.962
Amy and Claire felt like they were the only ones doing nothing.

00:28:48.022 --> 00:28:50.753
We've got to do something, Claire.

00:28:50.813 --> 00:28:51.613
Said Amy.

00:28:51.673 --> 00:28:53.604
Lisa's our best friend.

00:28:53.664 --> 00:28:54.754
You're right.

00:28:54.814 --> 00:28:56.545
Replied Claire.

00:28:56.605 --> 00:29:04.788
Before Inspector Swanson came back, they walked out of the police station and into the late afternoon.

00:29:04.848 --> 00:29:07.388
Which way do you think we should go?

00:29:07.448 --> 00:29:08.958
Left or right?

00:29:09.018 --> 00:29:12.638
asked Claire, looking down the busy street.

00:29:12.698 --> 00:29:15.049
Amy wasn't listening.

00:29:15.109 --> 00:29:17.820
She was looking at the photographs.

00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:20.021
They looked so happy.

00:29:20.081 --> 00:29:25.662
It was hard to believe that some of the photos were taken only a few days ago.

00:29:25.722 --> 00:29:28.644
Why do you think she didn't tell us?

00:29:28.704 --> 00:29:33.225
Claire turned around and realized that she was talking to herself.

00:29:33.285 --> 00:29:36.665
Amy, you're not listening to me at all.

00:29:36.725 --> 00:29:37.865
She complained.

00:29:37.925 --> 00:29:38.896
Mm-hmm.

00:29:38.956 --> 00:29:42.800
Said Amy, still distracted by the photos.

00:29:42.860 --> 00:29:48.194
There was something wrong, but she couldn't work out what it was.

00:29:48.254 --> 00:29:53.448
I said, why do you think Lisa didn't tell us that she has a famous dad?

00:29:53.509 --> 00:29:55.020
That's it!

00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:57.683
Shouted Amy, making Claire jump.

00:29:57.742 --> 00:29:58.824
Look!

00:29:58.884 --> 00:30:01.826
She said, showing the photos to Claire.

00:30:01.886 --> 00:30:02.774
What?

00:30:02.834 --> 00:30:05.313
It's just us three having fun.

00:30:05.373 --> 00:30:06.113
No!

00:30:06.173 --> 00:30:07.364
Look again!

00:30:07.424 --> 00:30:09.275
Insisted Amy.

00:30:09.335 --> 00:30:13.817
Claire took the photos from her and looked at them closely.

00:30:13.877 --> 00:30:16.488
But she couldn't see anything unusual.

00:30:16.548 --> 00:30:21.991
He's on this photo we took in Cairns and this one at Ayres Rock.

00:30:22.051 --> 00:30:26.393
He's even on photos that were taken before we came to Australia.

00:30:26.453 --> 00:30:27.363
Look!

00:30:27.423 --> 00:30:30.164
This one was taken at Heathrow Airport.

00:30:30.224 --> 00:30:31.048
Who?

00:30:31.108 --> 00:30:32.430
said Claire.

00:30:32.490 --> 00:30:35.292
She was starting to get impatient now.

00:30:35.352 --> 00:30:40.164
Amy wasn't making any sense and they didn't have time to waste like this.

00:30:40.224 --> 00:30:42.864
See, here in the background.

00:30:42.924 --> 00:30:45.406
That's more than a coincidence.

00:30:45.466 --> 00:30:51.682
Amy was pointing at the figure of a man with black hair in the background of the photos.

00:30:51.742 --> 00:30:53.617
He's followed us.

00:30:53.677 --> 00:30:56.639
He's the monster who has kidnapped Lisa.

00:30:56.699 --> 00:30:58.090
She said angrily.

00:30:58.150 --> 00:30:58.961
Amy.

00:30:59.021 --> 00:31:02.743
Said Claire, putting her hand on Amy's arm to calm her.

00:31:02.804 --> 00:31:04.575
I know that face.

00:31:04.635 --> 00:31:05.796
Jack.

00:31:05.856 --> 00:31:07.507
Interrupted Amy.

00:31:07.567 --> 00:31:09.928
But she wasn't looking at the photo.

00:31:09.988 --> 00:31:13.261
She was waving to a man across the street.

00:31:13.322 --> 00:31:15.883
Jack didn't see Amy.

00:31:15.943 --> 00:31:18.765
He walked quickly into a news agency.

00:31:18.825 --> 00:31:21.496
I thought he was leaving Sydney.

00:31:21.556 --> 00:31:24.106
She asked, turning to Claire.

00:31:24.166 --> 00:31:26.806
But Claire's face was white.

00:31:26.866 --> 00:31:29.397
You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:31:29.457 --> 00:31:30.768
Smile, Amy.

00:31:30.828 --> 00:31:34.299
Amy, the man in these photos.

00:31:34.359 --> 00:31:35.589
It's him.

00:31:35.649 --> 00:31:39.060
It's Jack!

00:31:39.120 --> 00:31:45.935
Chapter 7 The kidnappers' shadow.

00:31:45.995 --> 00:31:48.930
Don't be ridiculous, Claire.

00:31:48.990 --> 00:31:50.711
Jack's our friend.

00:31:50.771 --> 00:31:52.854
Loved Amy nervously.

00:31:52.914 --> 00:31:58.408
But before she looked at the photo again, she knew that Claire was right.

00:31:58.468 --> 00:32:00.731
Amy felt sick.

00:32:00.790 --> 00:32:02.992
Lisa liked Jack.

00:32:03.052 --> 00:32:04.844
She trusted him.

00:32:04.904 --> 00:32:07.106
They all thought he was nice.

00:32:07.166 --> 00:32:10.749
Look, he's coming out of the news agents now.

00:32:10.809 --> 00:32:11.900
Said Claire.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:13.858
I'm going to kill him.

00:32:13.918 --> 00:32:14.964
said Amy.

00:32:15.024 --> 00:32:17.135
She wanted to run over to him.

00:32:17.195 --> 00:32:19.225
But Claire stopped her.

00:32:19.285 --> 00:32:20.546
No.

00:32:20.606 --> 00:32:22.406
Don't be stupid.

00:32:22.466 --> 00:32:26.007
If you do that, we'll never find out where Lisa is.

00:32:26.067 --> 00:32:28.387
Let's follow him instead.

00:32:28.447 --> 00:32:30.708
We should phone the police though.

00:32:30.768 --> 00:32:34.108
Said Amy, taking her mobile phone out of her bag.

00:32:34.168 --> 00:32:35.479
There's no time.

00:32:35.539 --> 00:32:37.219
Said Claire.

00:32:37.279 --> 00:32:44.761
They started to follow him south through Hyde Park and then east down Oxford Street.

00:32:44.821 --> 00:32:50.923
He was walking fast and it was difficult not to lose sight of him in the busy street.

00:32:50.983 --> 00:33:01.566
It was still a public holiday and a lot of people were out enjoying the early evening sun and eating ice creams in the many bars of this lively neighborhood.

00:33:01.626 --> 00:33:03.206
Oh no!

00:33:03.266 --> 00:33:04.177
said Claire.

00:33:04.237 --> 00:33:05.496
What's the matter?

00:33:05.556 --> 00:33:06.746
asked Amy.

00:33:06.806 --> 00:33:12.558
She was staring at the back of Jack's head as he crossed the road a few steps in front of them.

00:33:12.618 --> 00:33:14.669
The traffic lights!

00:33:14.729 --> 00:33:16.700
What traffic lights?

00:33:16.760 --> 00:33:18.891
said Amy, confused.

00:33:18.951 --> 00:33:25.804
A tall woman with long brown hair stopped suddenly in front of her, obstructing her view.

00:33:25.864 --> 00:33:28.815
Amy wanted to push her out of the way.

00:33:28.875 --> 00:33:30.356
They're red!

00:33:30.416 --> 00:33:32.237
He's going to get away!

00:33:32.297 --> 00:33:33.632
said Amy.

00:33:33.692 --> 00:33:36.600
forced to stand still and wait.

00:33:36.660 --> 00:33:40.142
They watched Jack disappear into the crowd.

00:33:40.202 --> 00:33:45.734
It felt like an hour before the cars stopped and they could walk across the road.

00:33:45.794 --> 00:33:47.546
It's useless.

00:33:47.606 --> 00:33:48.576
Shouted Amy.

00:33:48.636 --> 00:33:50.618
We'll never find Lisa.

00:33:50.678 --> 00:33:52.508
We can't give up now.

00:33:52.568 --> 00:33:53.629
Said Claire.

00:33:53.689 --> 00:33:55.730
I'm going to the police station.

00:33:55.790 --> 00:33:58.902
Said Amy, refusing to go any further.

00:33:58.962 --> 00:34:05.970
But then, as she turned to go, she saw him again.

00:34:06.030 --> 00:34:10.568
Listening activity.

00:34:10.628 --> 00:34:12.528
1.

00:34:12.589 --> 00:34:16.470
I go here twice a week to play basketball.

00:34:16.530 --> 00:34:21.712
Because it's inside, we can play even when it's raining.

00:34:21.772 --> 00:34:23.354
2.

00:34:23.414 --> 00:34:28.436
I pass by here every morning so I can have something to read on the train.

00:34:28.497 --> 00:34:30.878
I like knowing what's happening in the world.

00:34:30.898 --> 00:34:33.200
3.

00:34:33.261 --> 00:34:37.693
It's only small but they have a really good choice of books.

00:34:37.753 --> 00:34:44.146
I love reading so I usually go once a week to take books back and borrow some more.

00:34:44.206 --> 00:34:45.916
4.

00:34:45.977 --> 00:34:50.519
We usually go here to see new films when they come out.

00:34:50.578 --> 00:34:54.200
We usually go at least twice a month.

00:34:54.260 --> 00:34:56.040
5.

00:34:56.100 --> 00:34:59.022
We've got a great one near our house.

00:34:59.082 --> 00:35:02.178
It's really big with lots of space.

00:35:02.238 --> 00:35:05.564
There are also lots of things for children to do.

00:35:05.624 --> 00:35:10.566
On a sunny day, I love going there to relax and read a book.

00:35:10.627 --> 00:35:12.277
6.

00:35:12.337 --> 00:35:18.630
My sister's travelling at the moment, and she seems to ask for something at least once a week.

00:35:18.690 --> 00:35:26.990
I always have to go to this place to send her things.

00:35:27.051 --> 00:35:40.846
The house was on a pretty street in Paddington, a residential district south of Sydney Harbour, not far from the youth hostel.

00:35:40.906 --> 00:35:47.062
It was a Victorian house and was identical to all the other houses on that street.

00:35:47.122 --> 00:35:53.426
Claire and Amy watched as Jack went through the gate and into the house.

00:35:53.486 --> 00:36:01.500
Once they were certain that nobody was watching them, they walked to the rear of the house and looked through a window.

00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:06.072
It was very dirty, but they could still see inside.

00:36:06.132 --> 00:36:12.388
The outside of the house was beautiful, but the inside was horrible.

00:36:12.448 --> 00:36:20.154
The furniture was ripped and empty tins of food, pizza boxes and cans were on the floor.

00:36:20.214 --> 00:36:24.835
Lisa was sitting on an old chair in the living room.

00:36:24.895 --> 00:36:29.868
Her hands were tied, and she looked frightened as she watched Jack.

00:36:29.928 --> 00:36:34.274
He was shouting, and his face was red with anger.

00:36:34.334 --> 00:36:38.188
For ten years I lived here, alone with my aunt.

00:36:38.248 --> 00:36:42.984
I couldn't even visit my dad, because he was in prison, in England.

00:36:43.044 --> 00:36:45.087
I'm sorry, I...

00:36:45.147 --> 00:36:47.930
said Lisa, trying to calm him down.

00:36:47.990 --> 00:36:48.962
No, you're not.

00:36:49.022 --> 00:36:50.253
You're not sorry.

00:36:50.313 --> 00:36:51.134
I am.

00:36:51.194 --> 00:36:56.990
No, you're sorry that you're not out with your friends, laughing and having fun as usual.

00:36:57.050 --> 00:36:59.433
Well, what about me?

00:36:59.493 --> 00:37:02.246
He screamed out of control.

00:37:02.306 --> 00:37:06.540
If you let me go, I won't tell anyone about this.

00:37:06.600 --> 00:37:08.248
Said Lisa desperately.

00:37:08.308 --> 00:37:10.636
Not Claire, not Amy.

00:37:10.696 --> 00:37:12.308
Nobody will ever know.

00:37:12.328 --> 00:37:14.590
It will be our secret.

00:37:14.650 --> 00:37:16.310
You're a liar.

00:37:16.370 --> 00:37:18.152
Just like you're dead.

00:37:18.212 --> 00:37:19.373
He screamed.

00:37:19.433 --> 00:37:22.165
So loud it made Amy and Claire jump.

00:37:22.225 --> 00:37:24.786
Do you think I could let you go now?

00:37:24.846 --> 00:37:26.898
After all this time?

00:37:26.958 --> 00:37:29.370
After all that he's done?

00:37:29.430 --> 00:37:31.542
My father was innocent.

00:37:31.602 --> 00:37:33.843
He told me he never did it.

00:37:33.903 --> 00:37:35.728
He was set up.

00:37:35.788 --> 00:37:38.813
Claire and Amy listened in silence.

00:37:38.873 --> 00:37:41.084
Too scared to breathe.

00:37:41.144 --> 00:37:46.136
He looked so different from this kind, funny guy they shared pizza with.

00:37:46.196 --> 00:37:48.538
This was the real Jack.

00:37:48.598 --> 00:37:51.269
I've planned this for a long time.

00:37:51.329 --> 00:37:55.041
I followed you and your stupid friends around Australia.

00:37:55.101 --> 00:37:57.216
And then you came to Sydney.

00:37:57.276 --> 00:38:01.573
When you argued with your friends on Bondi Beach, I was there.

00:38:01.633 --> 00:38:05.096
You knew me from the youth hostel and trusted me.

00:38:05.156 --> 00:38:08.368
And I could finally put my plan into action.

00:38:08.428 --> 00:38:10.980
Now your dad is going to pay.

00:38:11.040 --> 00:38:13.122
I hope he's got the money ready.

00:38:13.182 --> 00:38:14.983
Otherwise.

00:38:15.043 --> 00:38:23.460
He laughed a mad laugh in Lisa's face before rushing out of the house, locking the door behind him.

00:38:23.520 --> 00:38:26.474
Amy didn't wait one minute more.

00:38:26.534 --> 00:38:31.039
She took her mobile phone and dialed the number of the police station.

00:38:31.099 --> 00:38:32.090
Hello?

00:38:32.150 --> 00:38:35.132
Can I speak with Inspector Swanson, please?

00:38:35.192 --> 00:38:37.012
It's Amy Dixon.

00:38:37.072 --> 00:38:42.376
While Amy waited for Swanson to answer, Claire knocked on the window.

00:38:42.436 --> 00:38:43.576
Lisa!

00:38:43.636 --> 00:38:45.107
Shouted Claire.

00:38:45.167 --> 00:38:47.658
Everything's going to be okay.

00:38:47.718 --> 00:38:51.200
You're safe now.

00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:57.828
Chapter 9 Happy New Year."

00:38:57.888 --> 00:39:04.261
I still don't understand why you didn't tell us about your dad, said Claire.

00:39:04.321 --> 00:39:11.664
It was New Year's Eve, and Lisa's dad was paying for them to have dinner in an expensive restaurant.

00:39:11.724 --> 00:39:17.856
From their table, there was a fantastic view of Sydney Harbour and the Opera House.

00:39:17.916 --> 00:39:21.058
The night sky was full of stars.

00:39:21.118 --> 00:39:25.626
The nightmare of the past few days was finally over.

00:39:25.687 --> 00:39:28.675
I wanted you to like me for who I am.

00:39:28.735 --> 00:39:31.445
Not because my dad was a famous judge.

00:39:31.505 --> 00:39:32.736
Said Lisa.

00:39:32.796 --> 00:39:38.497
Well, I don't care if your dad is a judge or if he cleans the streets.

00:39:38.557 --> 00:39:40.367
What are you going to order?

00:39:40.427 --> 00:39:41.868
I can't decide.

00:39:41.928 --> 00:39:43.478
I'm so hungry.

00:39:43.538 --> 00:39:45.568
I could eat two of everything.

00:39:45.628 --> 00:39:46.669
Said Amy.

00:39:46.729 --> 00:39:49.529
We'll order some champagne first.

00:39:49.589 --> 00:39:50.910
Said Lisa's dad.

00:39:50.970 --> 00:39:52.888
I'm a lucky man.

00:39:52.948 --> 00:39:57.598
I always worried that something like this was going to happen.

00:39:57.658 --> 00:39:59.599
It's over now, Dad.

00:39:59.659 --> 00:40:05.860
Because of Amy and Claire, Jack's in prison, and he'll stay there for a long time.

00:40:05.920 --> 00:40:08.191
I want to get on with my life.

00:40:08.251 --> 00:40:11.472
Said Lisa, and she kissed him on the cheek.

00:40:11.532 --> 00:40:14.333
What are your new year's resolutions?

00:40:14.393 --> 00:40:15.793
Ask Amy.

00:40:15.853 --> 00:40:18.084
I'm going to give up chocolate.

00:40:18.144 --> 00:40:21.335
After I've tried that delicious looking chocolate cake.

00:40:21.395 --> 00:40:22.498
Said Claire.

00:40:22.558 --> 00:40:24.512
I'm going to retire.

00:40:24.572 --> 00:40:26.054
Said Lisa's dad.

00:40:26.114 --> 00:40:27.034
Why?

00:40:27.094 --> 00:40:28.615
You can't do that.

00:40:28.675 --> 00:40:31.057
Your job means everything to you.

00:40:31.117 --> 00:40:33.278
Said Lisa, surprised.

00:40:33.338 --> 00:40:36.510
I've thought about it for a long time.

00:40:36.571 --> 00:40:39.312
Even before all of this happened.

00:40:39.372 --> 00:40:42.455
I want to spend more time with my family.

00:40:42.515 --> 00:40:45.016
He said, smiling at Lisa.

00:40:45.076 --> 00:40:51.100
My new year's resolution is to remember my money and mobile phone when I go out.

00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:52.620
Laughed Lisa.

00:40:52.680 --> 00:40:53.981
Cheers!

00:40:54.041 --> 00:40:57.393
Laughed Amy, raising her glass.

00:40:57.453 --> 00:41:02.366
Dinner was delicious, and they all ate too much.

00:41:02.426 --> 00:41:06.508
Have you thought about what you are going to study at university?

00:41:06.568 --> 00:41:07.368
He asked.

00:41:07.428 --> 00:41:10.100
Oh Dad, don't be boring.

00:41:10.160 --> 00:41:11.830
It's New Year's Eve.

00:41:11.890 --> 00:41:14.482
There's lots of time to think about that.

00:41:14.542 --> 00:41:16.982
Said Lisa, suddenly nervous.

00:41:17.042 --> 00:41:20.564
Your future is very important.

00:41:20.624 --> 00:41:22.385
He said seriously.

00:41:22.445 --> 00:41:24.486
I know, but...

00:41:24.546 --> 00:41:29.128
Lisa knew that joining the police was what she definitely wanted.

00:41:29.188 --> 00:41:34.632
She also knew that sooner or later, she needed to tell her dad about her decision.

00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:37.292
But she didn't want to ruin this evening.

00:41:37.352 --> 00:41:39.754
She was having such a good time.

00:41:39.814 --> 00:41:40.985
Dad?

00:41:41.045 --> 00:41:42.426
She started.

00:41:42.486 --> 00:41:48.038
Taking a deep breath, she said the words she knew were going to disappoint him.

00:41:48.098 --> 00:41:52.200
I don't want to go to university.

00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:57.832
She avoided his eyes and waited for him to shout that she was making a big mistake.

00:41:57.892 --> 00:42:01.834
But when he spoke, his voice was warm.

00:42:01.894 --> 00:42:04.566
I know, he said.

00:42:04.626 --> 00:42:07.387
What do you mean I know?

00:42:07.447 --> 00:42:11.690
Lisa looked at him confused, but he was smiling.

00:42:11.750 --> 00:42:13.552
I'm your dad.

00:42:13.612 --> 00:42:19.478
I could see that whenever I talked about university, you looked unhappy.

00:42:19.538 --> 00:42:22.220
And what's important to me?

00:42:22.280 --> 00:42:25.422
He said, taking her hand gently in his.

00:42:25.482 --> 00:42:27.884
Is that your happy?

00:42:27.944 --> 00:42:31.036
So, can I join the police?

00:42:31.096 --> 00:42:33.257
If that's what you want.

00:42:33.317 --> 00:42:34.358
He smiled.

00:42:34.418 --> 00:42:36.029
Do you mean that?

00:42:36.089 --> 00:42:38.160
Asked Lisa, excitedly.

00:42:38.220 --> 00:42:41.046
She threw her arms around him.

00:42:41.107 --> 00:42:48.583
If Lisa is going to join the police, then you two could always become private investigators.

00:42:48.643 --> 00:42:50.924
He said, and Claire laughed.

00:42:50.984 --> 00:42:52.284
I'm serious.

00:42:52.344 --> 00:42:55.175
You found Lisa before the police did.

00:42:55.235 --> 00:42:59.596
But the girls were laughing too much to take him seriously.

00:42:59.656 --> 00:43:03.446
Here's to us, Charlie's Angels.

00:43:03.506 --> 00:43:06.047
Laugh, Lisa, making another toast.

00:43:06.107 --> 00:43:07.908
It'll soon be midnight.

00:43:07.968 --> 00:43:10.799
Shall we go outside with everyone else?

00:43:10.859 --> 00:43:14.332
At last, the countdown began.

00:43:14.392 --> 00:43:15.703
Ten.

00:43:15.764 --> 00:43:17.004
Nine.

00:43:17.064 --> 00:43:18.076
Eight.

00:43:18.136 --> 00:43:19.236
Seven.

00:43:19.296 --> 00:43:20.728
Everyone shouted.

00:43:20.788 --> 00:43:21.688
Six.

00:43:21.748 --> 00:43:22.759
Five.

00:43:22.819 --> 00:43:23.740
Four.

00:43:23.800 --> 00:43:24.731
Three.

00:43:24.791 --> 00:43:25.851
Two.

00:43:25.912 --> 00:43:26.912
One.

00:43:26.973 --> 00:43:29.404
Happy New Year!

00:43:29.464 --> 00:43:35.590
Fireworks filled the sky with loud bangs and a beautiful rainbow of color.

00:43:35.650 --> 00:43:38.864
Sydney was impressive at any time of year.

00:43:38.924 --> 00:43:43.478
But the harbor at New Year was unforgettable.

00:43:43.538 --> 00:43:48.020
Any plans for the future could wait until tomorrow.

00:43:48.080 --> 00:43:53.161
It was too good here and now.

00:43:53.221 --> 00:43:57.572
Listening activity.

00:43:57.632 --> 00:43:59.903
One.

00:43:59.963 --> 00:44:05.424
I thought it was silly when she wore high-heeled shoes to the beach.

00:44:05.484 --> 00:44:06.862
Two.

00:44:06.922 --> 00:44:09.152
He was really horrible.

00:44:09.212 --> 00:44:14.826
I mean, to be their friend, but all the time to be planning to kidnap Lisa.

00:44:14.886 --> 00:44:17.208
How could anyone do that?

00:44:17.268 --> 00:44:18.658
Three.

00:44:18.718 --> 00:44:24.343
He seems a nice man, but I don't think he's given much time to his family.

00:44:24.403 --> 00:44:27.525
His job was too important to him.

00:44:27.586 --> 00:44:29.328
Four.

00:44:29.388 --> 00:44:32.920
I don't feel that I know much about her, really.

00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:37.699
Only that she forgets things and that she wants to be a police woman.

00:44:37.759 --> 00:44:39.265
5.

00:44:39.325 --> 00:44:47.547
I think he was nice, but I don't understand why at first he thought Claire and Amy weren't being honest.

00:44:47.607 --> 00:44:49.548
6.

00:44:49.608 --> 00:44:54.079
I don't understand why she doesn't want to go to university.

00:44:54.139 --> 00:44:59.620
I mean, she could do that, then do the job she wants after her studies.

00:44:59.680 --> 00:45:01.201
7.

00:45:01.261 --> 00:45:04.482
She's the calm, sensible one, isn't she?

00:45:04.542 --> 00:45:07.832
The one who others depend on.

00:45:07.892 --> 00:45:11.034
I feel sorry for him.

00:45:11.094 --> 00:45:17.921
I mean, to be without his father for all those years, I can understand why he feels so angry.

